WEBVTT

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.560
We lost...

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.080
No...

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.800
The tournament's over for us...

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:20.910
Let the tears flow.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.510
Let it all out.

00:00:22.510 --> 00:00:24.980
It's okay to cry when you're upset.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:29.420
Cry your heart out, and then you can 
rise again tomorrow with a smile!

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.410
Sensei!

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.720
Sensei!

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.600
<i>Thank goodness their run
ended in the morning!</i>

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:48.550
<i>The rain's stopped too, so maybe I'll finally
get to go shopping this afternoon.</i>

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:49.600
Sensei.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:51.400
Yamaguchi-sensei.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:54.200
Uh, yes?

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:59.370
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:59.370
<b>Sakura Mutsuko</b>

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:59.370
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:59.370
<b>Shigeno Daigo</b>

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.330
The game's over.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:58.850
We're sorry. We won again.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.850
Oh, right. Impressive.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:03.580
So... we're in the final?

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:07.580
Yes, we'll watch Eihou's game
while we eat lunch,

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:09.150
then it's the final this afternoon.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.770
G-Got it.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.180
Please don't go home.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:18.970
<i>Crap. He knows I couldn't care less.</i>

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.880
Man, I seriously didn't see that one coming.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:55.900
<b>An Unexpected Reunion</b>

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.980
I mean, Sekitori causing the upset?

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:57.530
Who knew this mystery heavy 
hitter was a southpaw killer?

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:00.820
Even the Yokozuna Deliberation Committee
wouldn't have foreseen that one.

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:03.300
My name's not Sekitori! It's Kandori!

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:05.950
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:05.950
<b>Kandori Seira</b>

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.950
And stop working in sumo
references at every opportunity!

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:11.330
It's Eihou.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.460
Oh, it's the Fuurin team.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.510
Nice game. We were watching.
Congrats on getting to the final.

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:21.050
Oh, uh, thank you very much.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:25.500
Doing that with only nine players,
six of whom are girls, is quite something.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:26.830
Amazing, even.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:28.920
Are you the captain?

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:30.020
Yes.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:33.040
I heard Fuurin didn't have a coach,

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:36.140
which makes getting to the
final even more impressive.

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:39.250
We still have to get through
our semi-final game,

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:41.780
but if we win, I look forward
to a good game against you guys.

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:44.740
R-Right! We're looking forward to it, too!

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:46.740
Well, we'd better get going.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:47.950
Bye!

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.910
That coach was friendly, wasn't he?

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:54.800
I expected the coach of a 
powerhouse to be much scarier.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:58.890
He's the Jekyll and Hyde type, silly.
Nice off the field, total hard-ass in training.

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:00.380
Yikes, scary.

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:03.650
It's nice the rain stopped, though.

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:06.850
Woulda been much nicer
if it'd stopped a bit sooner.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.950
Good luck!

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:12.270
<b>Oobi</b>

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:12.270
<b>Eihou Academy</b>

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:12.270
<b>Eihou Academy</b>

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.980
Where are the guys?

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.240
The game's about to start.

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:17.630
And it's not like guys need more
than five minutes to change.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:19.070
Probably in the restroom.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.990
Sorry about that.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.320
Huh? Where are Daigo and Nishina?

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:27.450
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:27.450
<b>Tanba Hiromu</b>

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:27.450
They said they were going outside the park
to practice for a bit, since the rain's stopped.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:34.370
Apparently, that's more important 
than watching another Eihou game.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.480
Yeah, this patch of dirt will do. 
Try pitching from here.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:41.970
Why? It's still two hours till the game.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:44.380
It's way too early to warm up.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.050
This isn't a warm-up.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:49.600
We're going to hatch a plan
to rein in Eihou's batters.

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:55.160
Since it was raining yesterday, 
I didn't get to see your pitches.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:59.490
Your fastballs are great, but that
won't be enough to beat Eihou.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:02.940
A pitcher needs another type of pitch
to make his fastballs more effective.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.900
Another type?

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:06.650
It can just be for show.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:10.870
Let's find a breaking ball you're
comfortable with before the game begins.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:13.330
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:13.330
<b>Nishina Akira</b>

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.330
A-Are you serious?

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:20.000
Okay, let's start with a slider.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:31.640
G-Good. Well, we've confirmed
that it breaks.

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:34.600
Let's try that one more time.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.560
Here we... go!

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:41.400
Okay! Okay!

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:45.740
Let's forget sliders for now
and try a curveball.

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:51.140
Doesn't this seem... a bit weird?

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:52.030
Strike!

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:54.960
Yeah, something's off, all right.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:58.000
Maybe we should go fetch Professor Daigo.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:05.630
Oh, huh. You're not wearing your cup, Senpai?

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.590
Oh, there you are, Daigo!

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:11.180
Daigo, you gotta come see this!

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:15.930
I-I'm currently dealing with a pain
girls wouldn't understand...

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:20.020
Eihou's about to lose to Oobi, a no-name team!

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:26.360
<b>Oobi</b>

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:26.360
<b>Eihou Academy</b>

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:26.360
<b>Eihou Academy</b>

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:26.360
Wait, 2-0? And Eihou's only had one hit?

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:28.910
What's going on here?

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:34.010
Oobi Middle is a public school that
always loses in the first or second round.

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:38.680
<i>Does this mean Oobi's got a good pitcher?</i>

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:42.920
Strike!

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:47.120
Their starting pitcher's
small but that's fast.

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:50.510
That isn't their starting pitcher.
That's the reliever.

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:54.850
Their first pitcher is
the guy playing shortstop.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:59.810
He also has a fastball that's no joke, 
and he didn't give up a run in three innings.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:03.770
With that catcher who got two RBIs,

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:09.820
those three make up an elite trio who used to
play with Yayoi and Tao on Yokohama Little.

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:10.740
What?

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:13.200
You're out!

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:15.580
An elite trio from Yokohama Little?

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:19.910
Wouldn't they usually
join a local hardball team?

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:23.330
Why are they playing
middle school rubber-ball?

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:27.050
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:27.050
<b>Uozumi</b>

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:26.800
Did you notice the <i>other</i> thing
on the scoreboard, Daigo?

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.410
Check out the name of Oobi's 2-hole.

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:35.220
<b>Oobi</b>

