00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.290
<b>Yamamoto</b>

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.290
<b>Hirono</b>

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.290
<b>Ooshima</b>

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.290
<b>Tanaka</b>

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.290
<b>Oobi</b>

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.290
<b>Idemitsu</b>

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.290
<b>Mayumura</b>

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.290
<b>Seko</b>

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.290
<b>Uozumi</b>

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.290
<b>Hayazaka</b>

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.290
<b>Hada</b>

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.290
<b>Miura</b>

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.290
<b>Yamamuro</b>

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:08.290
<b>Kouda</b>

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:08.290
Seriously, those four jus'
beat Eihou by themselves.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:13.440
Idemitsu, Seko, Uozumi, 
and Mayumura Jr., huh?

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:17.670
It's not like they caused an upset.
They just came in under the radar.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:21.010
It really isn't a surprise they beat Eihou.

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:24.040
Our chances of beating them are zero.

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:34.570
<i>Michiru-chan...</i>

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:38.610
<i>I didn't expect to be facing 
off against you so soon.</i>

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:41.440
<i>It's just like Hikaru said.</i>

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:47.000
Thanks for coming, Daigo-kun.
I'm glad I got to see you.

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:49.630
Yeah, me too.

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:52.000
Next time, let's meet on the field...

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:56.550
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:56.550
<b>Satou Hikaru</b>

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:56.550
...is what I want to say, but let me heal up first.

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:58.030
Hikaru...

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:03.430
But I'm going to join my middle school 
baseball team and make a comeback.

00:11:04.300 --> 00:11:05.100
Yeah.

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:10.120
But since you're in Gunma and I'm in Kanagawa,
we're not exactly gonna see each other.

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:11.710
That's not true.

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:14.420
Sure, we're in different prefectures,

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:18.240
but if we keep winning, we'll see each other
at the Kanto Regionals or at Nationals.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:21.570
We might end up becoming rivals, though.

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:24.280
Yeah. You're right.

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:28.610
As long as we keep playing 
baseball, we <i>will</i> meet again.

00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:30.750
And it's not just us.

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:37.170
Mutsuko-chan, Urabe-kun, Andy, 
and the Mayumura twins...

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:41.850
As long as we love baseball and
keep playing it under the same sky,

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:43.430
we're guaranteed to meet again.

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:48.790
So let's carry on loving baseball forever.

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:50.170
Yeah!

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:52.350
And then, we'll get there.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:55.310
Yeah, we'll form...

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:00.530
...our invincible battery!

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:05.370
<i>As long as we carry on loving 
baseball under the same sky,</i>

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:07.680
<i>we're guaranteed to meet again, huh?</i>

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:14.400
<i>How long are you going to stare at her for?</i>

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:19.500
<i>It's been a while, Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:22.550
<i>I didn't expect to run into you in the final,</i>

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:25.610
<i>but unfortunately for you,
we won't hold back.</i>

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:30.220
<i>I'm going to keep moving
forward with my teammates.</i>

