00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:38.440
Yokohama Senior Training Ground

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:36.780
I'm Yamamoto Nobuyuki, first-year.

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:38.440
Nice to meet you!

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:40.200
Okay, next.

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:43.740
I'm Mayumura Michiru, first-year.

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:47.060
I pitched for the rubber-ball team, Touto Boys.

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:48.450
Nice to meet you!

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:53.350
A girl joining Senior
League from rubber-ball?

00:12:53.350 --> 00:12:59.130
Mayumura? That's Mayumura Ken's daughter,
I think. You know, the ex-Major Leaguer?

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:04.220
Well, I bet she'll find out just how hard 
real baseball is and run home crying.

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:08.180
What are you aiming at?

00:13:10.590 --> 00:13:14.390
What do ya think? My slider's 
gotten even better, hasn't it?

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:15.750
I guess.

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:20.650
What are you pitching for? 
You're in the outfield.

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:22.610
I'm just messing about, chill.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:26.360
Anyway, switching to pitcher in
Senior League sounds like a plan.

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:28.730
That way, me being a leftie might pay off.

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:29.570
What?

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:34.150
Looks like my fastball's faster than yours.

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:36.520
I think I'd make a better pitcher.

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:38.630
Huh? But you're a shortstop.

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.810
Uozumi, come with me.

00:13:40.810 --> 00:13:42.880
Come catch Mayumura's pitches.

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:44.090
Yes, sir.

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:49.760
Okay, let's see it.

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:53.720
All right, let's see the 
rubber-ball ace's pitches.

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:10.510
They're fast.

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:13.830
<i>They're not just fastballs, either.</i>

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:17.500
<i>She's got a variety of pitches, 
and her control's good, too.</i>

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:23.880
I never expected her to be that good.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:28.800
Now you've seen that, it's probably best
you forget about becoming a pitcher.

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:30.110
Shut up.

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:31.540
Same goes for you.

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:33.500
Hm, I'm not so sure about that.

00:14:34.130 --> 00:14:38.290
Mayumura and you guys have different styles,
so if you pitched one after another,

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:41.530
you'd keep the other team's batters
off-balance the entire game.

00:14:42.140 --> 00:14:43.580
You really believe that?

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:46.850
I see. Sounds like that
could be quite interesting.

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.330
We go to the same school?

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:57.020
Looks like.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:04.040
All right, next.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:05.900
Thanks!

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:07.510
Bring it!

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:14.560
Thanks!

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:18.030
Next.

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:27.460
Thanks.

00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:28.400
Next!

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.610
Ready!

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:44.250
Thanks!

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:48.560
Ready!

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:00.890
<b>Oobi Middle School</b>

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:00.890
<b>Oobi Middle School</b>

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:00.890
<b>Oobi Middle School</b>

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:01.660
What's her deal?

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:05.510
It's not just her pitching. Her batting, 
her fielding... She's perfect at everything.

00:16:05.510 --> 00:16:06.960
How's that even possible?

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:08.860
Was she really playing rubber-ball?

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:10.700
It's true.

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:14.410
The Touto Boys' Mayumura twins were famous.

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:16.240
Just admit it.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:19.780
We were wrong to underestimate her.

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:22.330
Hey, you guys.

00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:31.010
Our next practice is on the
south field. Where is it exactly?

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:34.260
You used it a lot when you
were in Yokohama Little, right?

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:40.880
Yeah, it's about 500 meters 
from our usual field.

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:43.980
It's a straight shot. You can't miss it.

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:46.050
I see. Thank you.

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:47.850
Mayumura.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:52.400
Why did you switch from
rubber-ball to Senior League?

00:16:53.750 --> 00:16:58.730
Because I felt like I'd get a truer
baseball experience, I guess.

00:17:02.970 --> 00:17:04.230
Yokohama.

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:06.540
Fight! Yeah! Fight! Yeah!

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:07.990
Yokohama.

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:10.500
Fight! Yeah! Fight! Yeah!

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:14.730
Yeah, you got this!

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:19.100
Crap!

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:22.890
Out!

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:31.960
Hey, let's hit the batting 
cages after school.

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:34.410
Okay, let's have another homerun battle.

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:36.510
Only if you bat right-handed.

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:42.280
You guys always wash up here, don't you?

00:17:42.280 --> 00:17:44.930
Hey, don't make it sound
like we're driftwood.

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:48.290
There's just no one else here
to talk about baseball with.

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:49.540
Huh.

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:53.220
We were talking about hitting 
the batting cages on our way home.

00:17:53.220 --> 00:17:54.370
Wanna tag along?

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:56.510
That's unexpected.

00:17:57.170 --> 00:18:00.900
I figured you thought I sucked
because I used to play rubber-ball.

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:02.890
Yeah, we did.

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:06.060
Until we saw you pitch, that is.

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.890
I mean, you can't deny your own eyes.

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:09.440
Exactly.

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:15.460
Man, it must be nice, though.

00:18:15.460 --> 00:18:18.790
Your ex-Major League dad 
is coaching you, right?

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:24.020
Nope, I haven't learned
a single thing from my dad.

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:25.870
Oh, really?

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:30.680
But isn't it nice to have someone
you want to emulate so close by?

00:18:30.680 --> 00:18:34.010
The pitcher I want to
emulate is Shigeno Goro!

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:36.460
That's been true since
the day I started playing.

00:18:36.710 --> 00:18:39.060
Shigeno Goro? That's unexpected.

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:41.930
Wait, shouldn't it still be your
dad who inspired you to play?

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:53.660
Nice ball!

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:56.360
Michiru's making some serious sounds.

00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:58.860
I think she got faster again.

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:02.220
Michiru, can I have a word?

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:03.120
Yes?

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:08.490
What do you mean, Coach?

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:13.210
I know you've worked really hard 
this last year since you joined us.

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:15.310
But you're a girl.

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:21.350
Basically, I don't consider
you an asset to the team.

00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:24.930
You don't consider me... an asset?

00:19:25.210 --> 00:19:29.430
You might be on the same level as the
boys right now, but it won't stay that way.

00:19:29.930 --> 00:19:33.980
From here on out, the guys 
will pull ahead of you physically.

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:36.150
That's just the way it is.

00:19:37.450 --> 00:19:38.690
No...

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:41.010
I'm sorry, Michiru.

00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:53.340
Is it true you quit Yokohama Senior?

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:55.760
Wataru.

00:19:57.580 --> 00:19:59.800
You heard about that, huh?

00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:04.630
I was told I'm not an asset. 
What other choice did I have?

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:07.100
Are you going to quit baseball completely?

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:12.520
There are ways to continue playing,
like going back to rubber-ball.

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:17.480
I can't think right now... about anything.

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:20.110
<b>Oobi Middle School</b>

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:20.110
<b>Oobi Middle School</b>

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:20.110
<b>Oobi Middle School</b>

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:40.990
Michiru!

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:44.320
You look bored.

00:20:47.230 --> 00:20:50.760
Wanna play baseball with us again?

00:20:50.760 --> 00:20:52.780
Let's play rubber-ball, win everything,

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:55.100
and show that coach just how wrong he was!

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:57.960
You're kidding, right?

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:00.120
You left Senior?

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:01.220
Really?

00:21:01.220 --> 00:21:02.820
Why would you do that?!

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:07.070
We just told you. To play baseball with you.

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:11.040
There was no reason for you guys to quit too!

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:12.660
You should go rejoin right now!

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:14.840
We don't want to.

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:18.750
We already made up our
minds to play rubber-ball.

00:21:20.450 --> 00:21:23.260
What? Why?

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:24.880
You said it yourself.

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:29.400
We felt this way, we'd get "a truer baseball
experience." That was it, wasn't it?

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:31.640
You're not gonna change our minds.

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:35.770
We have no intention of playing baseball
on a team you're not a part of.

00:21:39.320 --> 00:21:40.740
You guys...

00:21:43.470 --> 00:21:45.150
You're so stupid.

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:50.630
Thank you.

00:21:54.590 --> 00:21:55.980
What's wrong, Michiru?

00:21:56.840 --> 00:21:57.690
You know him?

00:21:57.690 --> 00:22:00.020
Oh, uh, yeah. Kinda.

00:22:00.020 --> 00:22:00.840
I see.

00:22:04.910 --> 00:22:06.180
<i>I won't lose!</i>

00:22:07.390 --> 00:22:08.640
<i>I can't lose!</i>

00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:13.760
<i>I need to repay those three
for what they did for me,</i>

00:22:13.760 --> 00:22:16.270
<i>going as far as leaving
Senior to be on my team.</i>

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:21.120
<i>As captain, in order to make Fuurin 
Middle's baseball team the best team ever,</i>

00:22:21.120 --> 00:22:24.890
<i>and to see Hikaru again, I need to do this!</i>

00:22:27.590 --> 00:22:28.960
<i>I'm going to win!</i>

00:22:27.590 --> 00:22:28.960
<i>I'm going to win!</i>

00:24:00.160 --> 00:24:04.710
Oobi Middle's good. With their ironclad 
defense, getting runs won't be easy.

00:24:04.870 --> 00:24:09.940
Okay. So I just need to use my monstrous
speed to get a perfect shutout, yeah?

00:24:09.940 --> 00:24:12.970
The problems will come mid-game,
when stamina starts running low.

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:15.760
Just rely on our fielders and throw strikes.

00:24:15.760 --> 00:24:20.560
Don't ya worry, they won't hit
a thing, so the fielders can relax.

00:24:19.970 --> 00:24:24.980
<b>Torn Feelings</b>

00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:22.320
Next time: "Torn Feelings."

00:24:22.320 --> 00:24:24.640
Run to the stage of your dreams!
